{"challenge_axes":["heldout_names","larger_graph_or_block_count"],"difficulty":4,"generation_seed":20261009,"generator_version":"1.3.2","oracle_version":"independent-1.0.0","record_hash":"78b99e6291a5d23811ffda0dd65dd885d53b93c1ce9ba3dcea1ae5e668b1d368","rendered_input":"Blocks contract: kind=blocks. on maps each distinct block name to a support block or TABLE. TABLE is reserved, supports must exist, and self-support, cycles, or more than one block directly on a block are malformed. TABLE may support several blocks. goal_on is a partial map using existing blocks or TABLE; self-support, cycles, and multiple blocks directly assigned to one block are contradictory and malformed. The initial state and goals here are well-formed. A block is clear when no block is directly on it. plan is an ordered list of {block,to} actions. A move is legal exactly when block exists and is clear, to is TABLE or an existing clear block distinct from block, and to differs from block's current support. A legal move changes only that block's support. At the first illegal move, include its {legal:false,after:unchanged_on_map} step, stop immediately, and ignore subsequent moves. An empty plan is valid. valid means every proposed move was legal. reaches_goal means the entire plan is valid and every goal_on entry equals the final on-map entry; unspecified supports need not change. shortest_plan is a fresh plan from the INITIAL on-map that satisfies every goal_on entry, minimizes the number of moves, and breaks ties by the lexicographic order of the complete sequence of (block,to) string pairs. It is [] when the initial state already satisfies the goal and null if unreachable. Return exactly a JSON object with steps:[{legal:boolean,after:on_map}], after:on_map, valid:boolean, reaches_goal:boolean, shortest_plan:list_or_null. Include only evaluated steps.\nTask JSON:\n{\"plan\":[{\"to\":\"sapphire\",\"block\":\"pearl\"},{\"to\":\"TABLE\",\"block\":\"quartz\"},{\"to\":\"quartz\",\"block\":\"ruby\"}],\"goal_on\":{\"onyx\":\"TABLE\",\"ruby\":\"quartz\",\"quartz\":\"TABLE\",\"pearl\":\"sapphire\",\"sapphire\":\"TABLE\"},\"on\":{\"sapphire\":\"TABLE\",\"pearl\":\"quartz\",\"quartz\":\"ruby\",\"ruby\":\"TABLE\",\"onyx\":\"TABLE\"},\"kind\":\"blocks\"}","renderer":"reverse","review_receipt_ids":["expert-RGM-001-expansion-v3-p0139-matched-reverse-3cd675df7065","adv-tags-4753704ba7084095c10ef3e3","adj-expansion-v3-a4c98315fafceb1de3ab"],"review_status":"ACCEPTED","reviewed_candidate_hash":"3cd675df706513022a4bfda1d3fff3b67805546fcbec71320f24f71b0d536fe1","sample_id":"RGM-001-expansion-v3-p0139-matched-reverse","semantic_family_id":"RGM-001-expansion-v3-p0139","semantic_parent_id":"RGM-001-expansion-v3-p0139","semantic_task":{"goal_on":{"onyx":"TABLE","pearl":"sapphire","quartz":"TABLE","ruby":"quartz","sapphire":"TABLE"},"kind":"blocks","on":{"onyx":"TABLE","pearl":"quartz","quartz":"ruby","ruby":"TABLE","sapphire":"TABLE"},"plan":[{"block":"pearl","to":"sapphire"},{"block":"quartz","to":"TABLE"},{"block":"ruby","to":"quartz"}]},"skill_tags":["relational_planning","state_transition","preconditions","canonical_shortest_plan","multiple_initial_table_stacks","blocks","matched_goal_outcome","valid_plan"],"source_family_key":"RGM-001-seed20261009-p0139","source_provenance":{"license":"repository-private-research","origin":"original_synthetic","sealed_evaluation_used":false},"split":"dev_challenge","structural_difficulty":4,"target_format":"structured","track_id":"RGM-001","verified_target":{"after":{"onyx":"TABLE","pearl":"sapphire","quartz":"TABLE","ruby":"quartz","sapphire":"TABLE"},"reaches_goal":true,"shortest_plan":[{"block":"pearl","to":"sapphire"},{"block":"quartz","to":"TABLE"},{"block":"ruby","to":"quartz"}],"steps":[{"after":{"onyx":"TABLE","pearl":"sapphire","quartz":"ruby","ruby":"TABLE","sapphire":"TABLE"},"legal":true},{"after":{"onyx":"TABLE","pearl":"sapphire","quartz":"TABLE","ruby":"TABLE","sapphire":"TABLE"},"legal":true},{"after":{"onyx":"TABLE","pearl":"sapphire","quartz":"TABLE","ruby":"quartz","sapphire":"TABLE"},"legal":true}],"valid":true}}
{"challenge_axes":[],"difficulty":4,"generation_seed":20261009,"generator_version":"1.3.2","oracle_version":"independent-1.0.0","record_hash":"f4d8257455f3ef897385143a5d6b2c081b13e8363cbe60b850c3a30506eff3fa","rendered_input":"Graph contract: kind=graph. nodes contains distinct strings. edges contains [from,to,cost] triples with positive integer fuel costs and at most one edge per ordered pair. start and goal are nodes; fuel is a nonnegative integer. plan is an ordered list of destination node names. Every edge is directed. Start at {node:start,fuel:fuel}. An action is legal exactly when an edge from the current node to its destination exists and its cost is at most the remaining fuel. A legal move changes node to its destination and subtracts the edge cost. At the first illegal action, include that action's {legal:false,after:unchanged_state} step, stop immediately, and do not evaluate subsequent actions. An empty plan is valid. valid means every proposed action was legal. reaches_goal is true exactly when the whole plan is valid and its terminal node is goal, including an initially satisfied goal with an empty plan. shortest_plan is a fresh plan from the INITIAL state that reaches goal within initial fuel, minimizes the number of moves, and breaks ties by the lexicographic order of the entire destination-name sequence. It is [] for an initially satisfied goal and null if no feasible plan exists. Fuel cost is a feasibility constraint, not the optimization objective. Return exactly a JSON object with steps:[{legal:boolean,after:{node:string,fuel:integer}}], after:{node:string,fuel:integer}, valid:boolean, reaches_goal:boolean, shortest_plan:list_or_null. Include only evaluated steps.\nTask JSON:\n{\"kind\":\"graph\",\"nodes\":[\"Ember\",\"Beryl\",\"Cedar\"],\"edges\":[[\"Ember\",\"Beryl\",3],[\"Beryl\",\"Cedar\",1],[\"Beryl\",\"Ember\",1]],\"start\":\"Ember\",\"goal\":\"Cedar\",\"fuel\":4,\"plan\":[\"Beryl\",\"Ember\",\"Beryl\",\"Ember\",\"Beryl\",\"Ember\",\"Beryl\