{"challenge_axes":[],"difficulty":2,"generation_seed":20261009,"generator_version":"1.3.2","oracle_version":"independent-1.0.0","record_hash":"e700fde987a8fcc7d57c171b03b88c33b12d1bce2990aa2cd38d7c47c1c474c1","rendered_input":"Blocks contract: kind=blocks. on maps each distinct block name to a support block or TABLE. TABLE is reserved, supports must exist, and self-support, cycles, or more than one block directly on a block are malformed. TABLE may support several blocks. goal_on is a partial map using existing blocks or TABLE; self-support, cycles, and multiple blocks directly assigned to one block are contradictory and malformed. The initial state and goals here are well-formed. A block is clear when no block is directly on it. plan is an ordered list of {block,to} actions. A move is legal exactly when block exists and is clear, to is TABLE or an existing clear block distinct from block, and to differs from block's current support. A legal move changes only that block's support. At the first illegal move, include its {legal:false,after:unchanged_on_map} step, stop immediately, and ignore subsequent moves. An empty plan is valid. valid means every proposed move was legal. reaches_goal means the entire plan is valid and every goal_on entry equals the final on-map entry; unspecified supports need not change. shortest_plan is a fresh plan from the INITIAL on-map that satisfies every goal_on entry, minimizes the number of moves, and breaks ties by the lexicographic order of the complete sequence of (block,to) string pairs. It is [] when the initial state already satisfies the goal and null if unreachable. Return exactly a JSON object with steps:[{legal:boolean,after:on_map}], after:on_map, valid:boolean, reaches_goal:boolean, shortest_plan:list_or_null. Include only evaluated steps.\nTask JSON:\n{\"plan\":[{\"to\":\"TABLE\",\"block\":\"amber\"}],\"goal_on\":{\"birch\":\"dahlia\",\"dahlia\":\"TABLE\",\"amber\":\"TABLE\"},\"on\":{\"birch\":\"TABLE\",\"dahlia\":\"cobalt\",\"cobalt\":\"amber\",\"amber\":\"TABLE\"},\"kind\":\"blocks\"}","renderer":"reverse","review_receipt_ids":["expert-RGM-001-expansion-v3-p0174-base-reverse-511224425c32","adv-tags-223ef8235b1d0431c553bdbd","adj-expansion-v3-95c13bb2925b1f5d99cd"],"review_status":"ACCEPTED","reviewed_candidate_hash":"511224425c323c85adc92bb2b76f1b7dec6d7ad07a99d4c406021e44088cd9db","sample_id":"RGM-001-expansion-v3-p0174-base-reverse","semantic_family_id":"RGM-001-expansion-v3-p0174","semantic_parent_id":"RGM-001-expansion-v3-p0174","semantic_task":{"goal_on":{"amber":"TABLE","birch":"dahlia","dahlia":"TABLE"},"kind":"blocks","on":{"amber":"TABLE","birch":"TABLE","cobalt":"amber","dahlia":"cobalt"},"plan":[{"block":"amber","to":"TABLE"}]},"skill_tags":["relational_planning","state_transition","preconditions","canonical_shortest_plan","multiple_initial_table_stacks","blocks","invalid_plan"],"source_family_key":"RGM-001-seed20261009-p0174","source_provenance":{"license":"repository-private-research","origin":"original_synthetic","sealed_evaluation_used":false},"split":"train","structural_difficulty":2,"target_format":"structured","track_id":"RGM-001","verified_target":{"after":{"amber":"TABLE","birch":"TABLE","cobalt":"amber","dahlia":"cobalt"},"reaches_goal":false,"shortest_plan":[{"block":"dahlia","to":"TABLE"},{"block":"birch","to":"dahlia"}],"steps":[{"after":{"amber":"TABLE","birch":"TABLE","cobalt":"amber","dahlia":"cobalt"},"legal":false}],"valid":false}}
{"challenge_axes":[],"difficulty":1,"generation_seed":20261009,"generator_version":"1.3.2","oracle_version":"independent-1.0.0","record_hash":"998e5edf0378a7d7ef5281d6b78066166046aa000811c2fc95869a1538ed8867","rendered_input":"Graph contract: kind=graph. nodes contains distinct strings. edges contains [from,to,cost] triples with positive integer fuel costs and at most one edge per ordered pair. start and goal are nodes; fuel is a nonnegative integer. plan is an ordered list of destination node names. Every edge is directed. Start at {node:start,fuel:fuel}. An action is legal exactly when an edge from the current node to its destination exists and its cost is at most the remaining fuel. A legal move changes node to its destination and subtracts the edge cost. At the first illegal action, include that action's {legal:false,after:unchanged_state} step, stop immediately, and do not evaluate subsequent actions. An empty plan is valid. valid means every proposed action was legal. reaches_goal is true exactly when the whole plan is valid and its terminal node is goal, including an initially satisfied goal with an empty plan. shortest_plan is a fresh plan from the INITIAL state that reaches goal within initial fuel, minimizes the number of moves, and breaks ties by the lexicographic order of the entire destination-name sequence. It is [] for an initially satisfied goal and null if no feasible plan exists. Fuel cost is a feasibility constraint, not the optimization objective. Return exactly a JSON object with steps:[{legal:boolean,after:{node:string,fuel:integer}}], after:{node:string,fuel:integer}, valid:boolean, reaches_goal:boolean, shortest_plan:list_or_null. Include only evaluated steps.\nTask JSON:\n{\"kind\":\"graph\",\"nodes\":[\"Dune\",\"Aster\",\"Ember\",\"Cedar\"],\"edges\":[[\"Dune\",\"Aster\",4],[\"Aster\",\"Ember\",1],[\"Ember\",\"Cedar\",4],[\"Ember\",\"Dune\",6],[\"Cedar\",\"Aster\",4]],\"start\":\"Dune\",\"goal\":\"Dune\",\"fuel\":9,\"plan\":[]}","renderer":