},\"kind\":\"blocks\"}","renderer":"reverse","review_receipt_ids":["expert-RGM-001-expansion-v3-p0177-base-reverse-69369eb9ded3","adv-tags-632dc43bee61ecae435b7d9a","adj-expansion-v3-23fe13fcda3f53dc2051"],"review_status":"ACCEPTED","reviewed_candidate_hash":"69369eb9ded3d45e17a3c1acb108120550312101e613cd576847aeb2b0ee2517","sample_id":"RGM-001-expansion-v3-p0177-base-reverse","semantic_family_id":"RGM-001-expansion-v3-p0177","semantic_parent_id":"RGM-001-expansion-v3-p0177","semantic_task":{"goal_on":{"birch":"cobalt","cobalt":"TABLE"},"kind":"blocks","on":{"amber":"TABLE","birch":"TABLE","cobalt":"birch"},"plan":[{"block":"cobalt","to":"TABLE"}]},"skill_tags":["relational_planning","state_transition","preconditions","canonical_shortest_plan","multiple_initial_table_stacks","blocks","valid_plan"],"source_family_key":"RGM-001-seed20261009-p0177","source_provenance":{"license":"repository-private-research","origin":"original_synthetic","sealed_evaluation_used":false},"split":"train","structural_difficulty":2,"target_format":"structured","track_id":"RGM-001","verified_target":{"after":{"amber":"TABLE","birch":"TABLE","cobalt":"TABLE"},"reaches_goal":false,"shortest_plan":[{"block":"cobalt","to":"TABLE"},{"block":"birch","to":"cobalt"}],"steps":[{"after":{"amber":"TABLE","birch":"TABLE","cobalt":"TABLE"},"legal":true}],"valid":true}}
{"challenge_axes":["heldout_names","larger_graph_or_block_count"],"difficulty":4,"generation_seed":20261009,"generator_version":"1.3.2","oracle_version":"independent-1.0.0","record_hash":"3c65cd7f4a91dd7702bee90f6c06fb952dab8be7e5bdcd93a6fa1938b1964dac","rendered_input":"Graph contract: kind=graph. nodes contains distinct strings. edges contains [from,to,cost] triples with positive integer fuel costs and at most one edge per ordered pair. start and goal are nodes; fuel is a nonnegative integer. plan is an ordered list of destination node names. Every edge is directed. Start at {node:start,fuel:fuel}. An action is legal exactly when an edge from the current node to its destination exists and its cost is at most the remaining fuel. A legal move changes node to its destination and subtracts the edge cost. At the first illegal action, include that action's {legal:false,after:unchanged_state} step, stop immediately, and do not evaluate subsequent actions. An empty plan is valid. valid means every proposed action was legal. reaches_goal is true exactly when the whole plan is valid and its terminal node is goal, including an initially satisfied goal with an empty plan. shortest_plan is a fresh plan from the INITIAL state that reaches goal within initial fuel, minimizes the number of moves, and breaks ties by the lexicographic order of the entire destination-name sequence. It is [] for an initially satisfied goal and null if no feasible plan exists. Fuel cost is a feasibility constraint, not the optimization objective. Return exactly a JSON object with steps:[{legal:boolean,after:{node:string,fuel:integer}}], after:{node:string,fuel:integer}, valid:boolean, reaches_goal:boolean, shortest_plan:list_or_null. Include only evaluated steps.\nTask JSON:\n{\"kind\":\"graph\",\"nodes\":[\"Sirocco\",\"Tundra\",\"Quasar\",\"Zephyr\",\"Obsidian\",\"Umber\",\"Vesper\",\"Nacre\"],\"edges\":[[\"Sirocco\",\"Tundra\",3],[\"Tundra\",\"Quasar\",1],[\"Quasar\",\"Zephyr\",2],[\"Zephyr\",\"Obsi